NAME
    play - WAV sound player for the desktop

SYNOPSIS
    play

DESCRIPTION
    A graphical sound player for the VNU desktop: lists the WAV
    clips in /etc/vnu/sounds, decodes the selected one with the embedded
    libwav parser and streams the PCM through the kernel's AC'97
    audio driver (audio_* syscalls). It is launched from the play
    tile on the desktop; the window is 480x340 and lives on the
    cooperative GUI scheduler, so audio_write is non-blocking and
    the ring is topped up on every heartbeat.

    The transport buttons and the space bar start (play), halt
    (pause), resume and stop playback; the progress bar tracks the
    play position via audio_pending() and the track's time is shown
    next to it. Pause keeps the position; resume restarts from there,
    stop rewinds to the beginning. The hardware plays 16-bit stereo,
    so 8-bit and/or mono clips are converted by the kernel driver.

KEYS
    Up / Down   select a clip
    Space       play / pause / resume
    s           stop
    Esc         close the window

FILES
    /etc/vnu/sounds     directory of embedded demo WAV clips
    /dev/dsp            the sound card as a byte stream (16-bit stereo PCM;
                        writes go straight to the AC'97 DMA ring)
    /apps/play/bin      the program itself

SYSCALLS
    audio_open, audio_set_fmt, audio_write, audio_pending, audio_pause,
    audio_reset, audio_close   the AC'97 playback channel
